  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nContinued dry conditions and near normal temperatures are\nanticipated Wednesday. Models depict a rebuilding of the upper \nridge into the region once again, reopening the door to warm \nsoutherly flow and the return of monsoon moisture by Thursday \nand Friday. Temperatures will become hot Thursday and Friday \nunder this pattern, with shower and thunderstorm chances \nincreasing both days. Meanwhile, a prominent, Pacific closed-\nlow will approach and move northeast through the PacNW beginning\nFriday, clipping the forecast area through the weekend. Showers\nand thunderstorm chances will persevere as the trough enhances \nlarge-scale lift and carries moisture. Several degrees of \ncooling will be likely for Saturday and Sunday.",
